{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011cFN5699fAVctGu1aziH5W","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//! Test cases for `picoquictest/dualq_aqm_test.c`.\n2\t//!\n3\t//! Unit tests for the DualQ Coupled AQM (RFC 9332) implementation used\n4\t//! in the network simulator.  The test suite is structured as five\n5\t//! sequential sub-tests:\n6\t//!\n7\t//! 1. `dualq_ctx_test`   — create / release the context.\n8\t//! 2. `dualq_enqueue`    — verify the per-queue enqueue API.\n9\t//! 3. `dualq_dequeue`    — verify the dequeue scheduler.\n10\t//! 4. `dualq_submit`     — verify submit routing and drop-on-overflow.\n11\t//! 5. `dualq_sustain`    — end-to-end throughput with mixed ECN traffic.\n12\t\n13\t#![allow(non_snake_case)]\n14\t\n15\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n16\t// Sub-test helpers.  Each mirrors one C helper function; all are `todo!()`\n17\t// until Phase 4 implements the simulation infrastructure.\n18\t\n19\t/// Verify that `test_set_minimal_cnx_with_time` + `TestSimLink::create` +\n20\t/// `Dualq::install` complete without error.\n21\t/// C: `dualq_test_ctx_test`.\n22\tfn dualq_ctx_test() -> crate::Result<()> {\n23\t    todo!(\"dualq_ctx_test: minimal-cnx and link creation not yet implemented\")\n24\t}\n25\t\n26\t/// Enqueue one packet per ECN value into the matching queue and verify\n27\t/// that `queue_bytes`, head, and tail pointers update correctly.\n28\t/// C: `dualq_enqueue_test`.\n29\tfn dualq_enqueue() -> crate::Result<()> {\n30\t    todo!(\"dualq_enqueue: queue field inspection not yet implemented\")\n31\t}\n32\t\n33\t/// Load five packets, dequeue until both queues are empty, and verify\n34\t/// all five packets are delivered within 100 ms simulated time.\n35\t/// C: `dualq_dequeue_test`.\n36\tfn dualq_dequeue() -> crate::Result<()> {\n37\t    todo!(\"dualq_dequeue: dequeue loop not yet implemented\")\n38\t}\n39\t\n40\t/// Submit 50 packets and verify that: the first packet goes directly to\n41\t/// the link when the link queue is idle; subsequent packets go to the AQM\n42\t/// queues; and at least one packet is dropped when the combined queue\n43\t/// exceeds `dqs.limit`.\n44\t/// C: `dualq_submit_test`.\n45\tfn dualq_submit() -> crate::Result<()> {\n46\t    todo!(\"dualq_submit: link submit routing not yet implemented\")\n47\t}\n48\t\n49\t/// Drive 100 mixed-ECN packets through the full submit→dequeue pipeline,\n50\t/// interleaving arrivals, admissions, and submissions; verify all 100 are\n51\t/// accounted for (received + dropped) within 125 ms simulated time.\n52\t/// C: `dualq_sustain_test`.\n53\tfn dualq_sustain() -> crate::Result<()> {\n54\t    todo!(\"dualq_sustain: end-to-end loop not yet implemented\")\n55\t}\n56\t\n57\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n58\t// Test entry.\n59\t\n60\t/// Run the full DualQ AQM unit-test suite.\n61\t/// C: `dualq_aqm_test` in `picoquictest/dualq_aqm_test.c`.\n62\t#[test]\n63\tfn dualq_aqm() {\n64\t    dualq_ctx_test().expect(\"dualq_ctx_test\");\n65\t    dualq_enqueue().expect(\"dualq_enqueue\");\n66\t    dualq_dequeue().expect(\"dualq_dequeue\");\n67\t    dualq_submit().expect(\"dualq_submit\");\n68\t    dualq_sustain().expect(\"dualq_sustain\");\n69\t}\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efe36d5e-8c7a-42d9-a085-8d43da824da0","uuid":"ee0a8412-6c14-41b8-9af8-5c2bf14b1a39","timestamp":"2026-05-05T03:52:18.643Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/src/tests/dualq_aqm.rs","content":"//! Test cases for `picoquictest/dualq_aqm_test.c`.\n//!\n//! Unit tests for the DualQ Coupled AQM (RFC 9332) implementation used\n//! in the network simulator.  The test suite is structured as five\n//! sequential sub-tests:\n//!\n//! 1. `dualq_ctx_test`   — create / release the context.\n//! 2. `dualq_enqueue`    — verify the per-queue enqueue API.\n//! 3. `dualq_dequeue`    — verify the dequeue 