{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HMYxfiKd7Tnsgbz22x978q","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"phase3_check.py — verify that every C test in the named source\n3\tfiles has a translated Rust body.\n4\t\n5\tUsage:\n6\t  python3 scripts/phase3_check.py                     # check all sources\n7\t  python3 scripts/phase3_check.py sacktest config_test # check named sources\n8\t\n9\tExit code 0 if every test has a real body; non-zero otherwise.\n10\t\n11\tA test counts as \"translated\" when its `#[test] fn <name>()` body\n12\tin `rs/fq/src/tests/<rust>.rs` is anything other than the bare\n13\tauto-stub pattern:\n14\t\n15\t    #[test]\n16\t    fn <name>() {\n17\t        todo!(\"<entry_fn>\")\n18\t    }\n19\t\n20\tTests with a non-todo body (assertions, real calls, even an\n21\texplicit `todo!()` followed by a comment / multiple lines that\n22\t*do* make the test signal richer) all count as translated.\n23\t\n24\tThe script reads `picoquic_t/picoquic_t.c`'s `test_table[]` and\n25\tthe `xlate/prompts/phase3a/<src>.md` files (which list each\n26\tsource's expected entries) to know which `#[test] fn` names to\n27\texpect in each `tests/<rust>.rs`.\n28\t\"\"\"\n29\t\n30\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n31\t\n32\timport argparse\n33\timport re\n34\timport sys\n35\tfrom collections import defaultdict\n36\tfrom pathlib import Path\n37\t\n38\tREPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n39\tDRIVER = REPO_ROOT / \"picoquic_t\" / \"picoquic_t.c\"\n40\tPICOQUICTEST = REPO_ROOT / \"picoquictest\"\n41\tRS_TESTS = REPO_ROOT / \"rs\" / \"fq\" / \"src\" / \"tests\"\n42\t\n43\t# Same map as phase3a.py.\n44\tRUST_FILENAME_OVERRIDES = {\n45\t    \"util_test\": \"util_test\",\n46\t}\n47\t\n48\tRUST_KEYWORDS = {\n49\t    \"as\", \"break\", \"const\", \"continue\", \"crate\", \"else\", \"enum\", \"extern\",\n50\t    \"false\", \"fn\", \"for\", \"if\", \"impl\", \"in\", \"let\", \"loop\", \"match\", \"mod\",\n51\t    \"move\", \"mut\", \"pub\", \"ref\", \"return\", \"self\", \"Self\", \"static\", \"struct\",\n52\t    \"super\", \"trait\", \"true\", \"type\", \"unsafe\", \"use\", \"where\", \"while\",\n53\t    \"async\", \"await\", \"dyn\", \"abstract\", \"become\", \"box\", \"do\", \"final\",\n54\t    \"macro\", \"override\", \"priv\", \"typeof\", \"unsized\", \"virtual\", \"yield\",\n55\t    \"try\",\n56\t}\n57\t\n58\t\n59\tdef sanitize_test_name(name: str) -> str:\n60\t    out = re.sub(r\"[^A-Za-z0-9_]\", \"_\", name).lower()\n61\t    if not out:\n62\t        out = \"test\"\n63\t    if out[0].isdigit():\n64\t        out = \"_\" + out\n65\t    if out in RUST_KEYWORDS:\n66\t        out = f\"r#{out}\"\n67\t    return out\n68\t\n69\t\n70\tdef rust_filename_for(src: str) -> str:\n71\t    if src in RUST_FILENAME_OVERRIDES:\n72\t        return RUST_FILENAME_OVERRIDES[src]\n73\t    name = src\n74\t    for suffix in (\"_tests\", \"_test\"):\n75\t        if name.endswith(suffix):\n76\t            name = name[: -len(suffix)]\n77\t            break\n78\t    return name\n79\t\n80\t\n81\tdef parse_test_table() -> list[tuple[str, str]]:\n82\t    text = DRIVER.read_text()\n83\t    start = re.search(r\"static const \\S+ test_table\\[\\]\\s*=\\s*\\{\", text)\n84\t    if not start:\n85\t        raise SystemExit(\"error: test_table[] not found\")\n86\t    row_pat = re.compile(\n87\t        r\"\\{\\s*\\\"(?P<name>[^\\\"]+)\\\"\\s*,\\s*(?P<fn>[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\\s*\\}\",\n88\t    )\n89\t    rows: list[tuple[str, str]] = []\n90\t    pos = start.end()\n91\t    while True:\n92\t        end = text.find(\"};\", pos)\n93\t        m = row_pat.search(text, pos, end if end > 0 else None)\n94\t        if not m:\n95\t            break\n96\t        rows.append((m.group(\"name\"), m.group(\"fn\")))\n97\t        pos = m.end()\n98\t    return rows\n99\t\n100\t\n101\tdef index_entry_fns() -> dict[str, str]:\n102\t    fn_to_src: dict[str, str] = {}\n103\t    pat = re.compile(\n104\t        r\"^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_ \\t\\*]*\\b([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\\s*\\([^;]*?\\)\\s*\\{\",\n105\t        re.MULTILINE | re.DOTALL,\n106\t    )\n107\t    sources = sorted(PICOQUICTEST.glob(\"*.c\")) + sorted(PICOQUICTEST.glob(\"*.cpp\"))\n108\t    for src in sources:\n109\t        text = src.read_text(errors=\"replace\")\n110\t        for m in pat.finditer(text):\n111\t            fn = m.group(1)\n112\t            if fn in fn_to_src or fn in {\n113\t                \"if\", \"while\", \"for\", \"switch\", \"return\", \"do\", \"else\",\n114\t                \"case\", \"default\", \"break\", \"continue\", \"goto\", \"sizeof\",\n115\t            }:\n116\t                continue\n117\t            fn_to_src[fn] = src.stem\n118\t    fn_to_src.setdefault(\"cplusplustest\", \"cplusplus\")\n119\t    fn_to_src.setdefault(\"sim_link_test\", \"<harness>\")\n120\t    return fn_to_src\n121\t\n122\t\n123\tdef group_by_source() -> dict[str, list[tuple[str, str]]]:\n124\t    rows = parse_test_table()\n125\t    fn_to_src = index_entry_fns()\n126\t    by_src: dict[str, list[tuple[str, str]]] = defaultdict(list)\n127\t    for name, fn in rows:\n128\t        src = fn_to_src.get(fn, \"<unknown>\")\n129\t        if src.startswith(\"<\"):\n130\t            continue\n131\t        by_src[src].append((name, fn))\n132\t    return dict(by_src)\n133\t\n134\t\n135\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n136\t# The actual check: parse a Rust test file and return the set of\n137\t# `#[test] fn` names whose bodies are still the auto-stub.\n138\t\n139\t# Match the bare auto-stub: `#[test]\\nfn <name>() {\\n    todo!(\"<fn>\")\\n}`.\n140\t# Tolerant of extra `#[allow(...)]` lines above and minor formatting.\n141\tSTUB_RE = re.compile(\n142\t    r\"#\\[test\\]\\s*\\n\"                       # the attribute\n143\t    r\"\\s*fn\\s+(?P<name>[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_#]*)\\s*\\(\\s*\\)\\s*\\{\\s*\"\n144\t    r\"todo!\\s*\\(\\s*\\\"[^\\\"]*\\\"\\s*\\)\\s*\\n?\\s*\\}\",\n145\t    re.MULTILINE,\n146\t)\n147\t\n148\t# Regex that finds *every* `#[test] fn <name>` declaration so we can\n149\t# verify the file even has the test (we don't want to accept \"test\n150\t# missing entirely\" as success).\n151\tTEST_DECL_RE = re.compile(\n152\t    r\"#\\[test\\]\\s*\\n\\s*fn\\s+(?P<name>[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_#]*)\\s*\\(\",\n153\t    re.MULTILINE,\n154\t)\n155\t\n156\t\n157\tdef stub_names_in(rust_path: Path) -> set[str]:\n158\t    text = rust_path.read_text()\n159\t    return {m.group(\"name\") for m in STUB_RE.finditer(text)}\n160\t\n161\t\n162\tdef declared_names_in(rust_path: Path) -> set[str]:\n163\t    text = rust_path.read_text()\n164\t    return {m.group(\"name\") for m in TEST_DECL_RE.finditer(text)}\n165\t\n166\t\n167\tdef check_source(src: str, by_src: dict[str, list[tuple[str, str]]]) -> tuple[int, list[str]]:\n168\t    \"\"\"Return (missing_count, lines) where lines is human-readable.\"\"\"\n169\t    rust_path = RS_TESTS / f\"{rust_filename_for(src)}.rs\"\n170\t    if not rust_path.exists():\n171\t        return 1, [f\"  {src}: missing test file at {rust_path.relative_to(REPO_ROOT)}\"]\n172\t    expected = {sanitize_test_name(name): fn for name, fn in by_src.get(src, [])}\n173\t    if not expected:\n174\t        return 1, [f\"  {src}: no entries known\"]\n175\t    declared = declared_names_in(rust_path)\n176\t    stubbed = stub_names_in(rust_path)\n177\t    issues: list[str] = []\n178\t    for ident, fn in sorted(expected.items()):\n179\t        if ident not in declared:\n180\t            issues.append(f\"  {src}::{ident} (C `{fn}`): MISSING `#[test] fn`\")\n181\t        elif ident in stubbed:\n182\t            issues.append(f\"  {src}::{ident} (C `{fn}`): still a `todo!()` stub\")\n183\t    return len(issues), issues\n184\t\n185\t\n186\tdef main() -> int:\n187\t    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__,\n188\t                                formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)\n189\t    p.add_argument(\"sources\", nargs=\"*\",\n190\t                   help=\"Source basenames (e.g. sacktest, config_test).  \"\n191\t                        \"Default: all 56 sources.\")\n192\t    p.add_argument(\"--quiet\", action=\"store_true\",\n193\t                   help=\"Print only sources with missing translations.\")\n194\t    args = p.parse_args()\n195\t\n196\t    by_src = group_by_source()\n197\t    targets = args.sources if args.sources else sorted(by_src.keys())\n198\t\n199\t    total_missing = 0\n200\t    total_done = 0\n201\t    issues_by_src: dict[str, list[str]] = {}\n202\t    for src in targets:\n203\t        if src not in by_src:\n204\t            print(f\"WARNING: unknown source {src!r}\", file=sys.stderr)\n205\t            continue\n206\t        missing, lines = check_source(src, by_src)\n207\t        total_missing += missing\n208\t        if missing == 0:\n209\t            total_done += 1\n210\t            if not args.quiet:\n211\t                print(f\"OK    {src}\")\n212\t        else:\n213\t            issues_by_src[src] = lines\n214\t            print(f\"FAIL  {src}  ({missing} missing)\")\n215\t\n216\t    if issues_by_src:\n217\t        print(\"\\nDetails:\")\n218\t        for src, lines in sorted(issues_by_src.items()):\n219\t            for line in lines:\n220\t                print(line)\n221\t\n222\t    print(f\"\\nSummary: {total_done}/{len(targets)} sources fully translated.  \"\n223\t          f\"{total_missing} test stubs still need bodies.\")\n224\t    return 0 if total_missing == 0 else 1\n225\t\n226\t\n227\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n228\t    sys.exit(main())\n229\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efe36d5e-8c7a-42d9-a085-8d43da824da0","uuid":"acc0faba-cc3f-4393-b98f-2b3cb868c82b","timestamp":"2026-05-05T03:54:56.710Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/scripts/phase3_check.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"phase3_check.py — verify that every C test in the named source\nfiles has a translated Rust body.\n\nUsage:\n  python3 scripts/phase3_check.py                     # check all sources\n  python3 scripts/phase3_check.py sacktest config_test # check named sources\n\nExit code 0 if every test has a real body; non-zero otherwise.\n\nA test counts as \"translated\" when its `#[test] fn <name>()` body\nin `rs/fq/src/tests/<rust>.rs` is anything other than the bare\nauto-stub pattern:\n\n    #[test]\n    fn <name>() {\n        todo!(\"<entry_fn>\")\n    }\n\nTests with a non-todo body (assertions, real calls, even an\nexplicit `todo!()` followed by a comment / multiple lines that\n*do* make the test signal richer) all count as translated.\n\nThe script reads `picoquic_t/picoquic_t.c`'s `test_table[]` and\nthe `xlate/prompts/phase3a/<src>.md` files (which list each\nsource's expected entries) to know which `#[test] fn` names to\nexpect in each `tests/<rust>.rs`.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nREPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nDRIVER = REPO_ROOT / \"picoquic_t\" / \"picoquic_t.c\"\nPICOQUICTEST = REPO_ROOT / \"picoquictest\"\nRS_TESTS = REPO_ROOT / \"rs\" / \"fq\" / \"src\" / \"tests\"\n\n# Same map as phase3a.py.\nRUST_FILENAME_OVERRIDES = {\n    \"util_test\": \"util_test\",\n}\n\nRUST_KEYWORDS = {\n    \"as\", \"break\", \"const\", \"continue\", \"crate\", \"else\", \"enum\", \"extern\",\n    \"false\", \"fn\", \"for\", \"if\", \"impl\", \"in\", \"let\", \"loop\", \"match\", \"mod\",\n    \"move\", \"mut\", \"pub\", \"ref\", \"return\", \"self\", \"Self\", \"static\", \"struct\",\n    \"super\", \"trait\", \"true\", \"type\", \"unsafe\", \"use\", \"where\", \"while\",\n    \"async\", \"await\", \"dyn\", \"abstract\", \"become\", \"box\", \"do\", \"final\",\n    \"macro\", \"override\", \"priv\", \"typeof\", \"unsized\", \"virtual\", \"yield\",\n    \"try\",\n}\n\n\ndef sanitize_test_name(name: str) -> str:\n    out = re.sub(r\"[^A-Za-z0-9_]\", \"_\", name).lower()\n    if not out:\n        out = \"test\"\n    if out[0].isdigit():\n        out = \"_\" + out\n    if out in RUST_KEYWORDS:\n        out = f\"r#{out}\"\n    return out\n\n\ndef rust_filename_for(src: str) -> str:\n    if src in RUST_FILENAME_OVERRIDES:\n        return RUST_FILENAME_OVERRIDES[src]\n    name = src\n    for suffix in (\"_tests\", \"_test\"):\n        if name.endswith(suffix):\n            name = name[: -len(suffix)]\n            break\n    return name\n\n\ndef parse_test_table() -> list[tuple[str, str]]:\n    text = DRIVER.read_text()\n    start = re.search(r\"static const \\S+ test_table\\[\\]\\s*=\\s*\\{\", text)\n    if not start:\n        raise SystemExit(\"error: test_table[] not found\")\n    row_pat = re.compile(\n        r\"\\{\\s*\\\"(?P<name>[^\\\"]+)\\\"\\s*,\\s*(?P<fn>[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\\s*\\}\",\n    )\n    rows: list[tuple[str, str]] = []\n    pos = start.end()\n    while True:\n        end = text.find(\"};\", pos)\n        m = row_pat.search(text, pos, end if end > 0 else None)\n        if not m:\n            break\n        rows.append((m.group(\"name\"), m.group(\"fn\")))\n        pos = m.end()\n    return rows\n\n\ndef index_entry_fns() -> dict[str, str]:\n    fn_to_src: dict[str, str] = {}\n    pat = re.compile(\n        r\"^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_ \\t\\*]*\\b([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)\\s*\\([^;]*?\\)\\s*\\{\",\n        re.MULTILINE | re.DOTALL,\n    )\n    sources = sorted(PICOQUICTEST.glob(\"*.c\")) + sorted(PICOQUICTEST.glob(\"*.cpp\"))\n    for src in sources:\n        text = src.read_text(errors=\"replace\")\n        for m in pat.finditer(text):\n            fn = m.group(1)\n            if fn in fn_to_src or fn in {\n                \"if\", \"while\", \"for\", \"switch\", \"return\", \"do\", \"else\",\n                \"case\", \"default\", \"break\", \"continue\", \"goto\", \"sizeof\",\n            }:\n                continue\n            fn_to_src[fn] = src.stem\n    fn_to_src.setdefault(\"cplusplustest\", \"cplusplus\")\n    fn_to_src.setdefault(\"sim_link_test\", \"<harness>\")\n    return fn_to_src\n\n\ndef group_by_source() -> dict[str, list[tuple[str, str]]]:\n    rows = parse_test_table()\n    fn_to_src = index_entry_fns()\n    by_src: dict[str, list[tuple[str, str]]] = defaultdict(list)\n    for name, fn in rows:\n        src = fn_to_src.get(fn, \"<unknown>\")\n        if src.startswith(\"<\"):\n            continue\n        by_src[src].append((name, fn))\n    return dict(by_src)\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# The actual check: parse a Rust test file and return the set of\n# `#[test] fn` names whose bodies are still the auto-stub.\n\n# Match the bare auto-stub: `#[test]\\nfn <name>() {\\n    todo!(\"<fn>\")\\n}`.\n# Tolerant of extra `#[allow(...)]` lines above and minor formatting.\nSTUB_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"#\\[test\\]\\s*\\n\"                       # the attribute\n    r\"\\s*fn\\s+(?P<name>[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_#]*)\\s*\\(\\s*\\)\\s*\\{\\s*\"\n    r\"todo!\\s*\\(\\s*\\\"[^\\\"]*\\\"\\s*\\)\\s*\\n?\\s*\\}\",\n    re.MULTILINE,\n)\n\n# Regex that finds *every* `#[test] fn <name>` declaration so we can\n# verify the file even has the test (we don't want to accept \"test\n# missing entirely\" as success).\nTEST_DECL_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"#\\[test\\]\\s*\\n\\s*fn\\s+(?P<name>[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_#]*)\\s*\\(\",\n    re.MULTILINE,\n)\n\n\ndef stub_names_in(rust_path: Path) -> set[str]:\n    text = rust_path.read_text()\n    return {m.group(\"name\") for m in STUB_RE.finditer(text)}\n\n\ndef declared_names_in(rust_path: Path) -> set[str]:\n    text = rust_path.read_text()\n    return {m.group(\"name\") for m in TEST_DECL_RE.finditer(text)}\n\n\ndef check_source(src: str, by_src: dict[str, list[tuple[str, str]]]) -> tuple[int, list[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Return (missing_count, lines) where lines is human-readable.\"\"\"\n    rust_path = RS_TESTS / f\"{rust_filename_for(src)}.rs\"\n    if not rust_path.exists():\n        return 1, [f\"  {src}: missing test file at {rust_path.relative_to(REPO_ROOT)}\"]\n    expected = {sanitize_test_name(name): fn for name, fn in by_src.get(src, [])}\n    if not expected:\n        return 1, [f\"  {src}: no entries known\"]\n    declared = declared_names_in(rust_path)\n    stubbed = stub_names_in(rust_path)\n    issues: list[str] = []\n    for ident, fn in sorted(expected.items()):\n        if ident not in declared:\n            issues.append(f\"  {src}::{ident} (C `{fn}`): MISSING `#[test] fn`\")\n        elif ident in stubbed:\n            issues.append(f\"  {src}::{ident} (C `{fn}`): still a `todo!()` stub\")\n    return len(issues), issues\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__,\n                                formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)\n    p.add_argument(\"sources\", nargs=\"*\",\n                   help=\"Source basenames (e.g. sacktest, config_test).  \"\n                        \"Default: all 56 sources.\")\n    p.add_argument(\"--quiet\", action=\"store_true\",\n                   help=\"Print only sources with missing translations.\")\n    args = p.parse_args()\n\n    by_src = group_by_source()\n    targets = args.sources if args.sources else sorted(by_src.keys())\n\n    total_missing = 0\n    total_done = 0\n    issues_by_src: dict[str, list[str]] = {}\n    for src in targets:\n        if src not in by_src:\n            print(f\"WARNING: unknown source {src!r}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            continue\n        missing, lines = check_source(src, by_src)\n        total_missing += missing\n        if missing == 0:\n            total_done += 1\n            if not args.quiet:\n                print(f\"OK    {src}\")\n        else:\n            issues_by_src[src] = lines\n            print(f\"FAIL  {src}  ({missing} missing)\")\n\n    if issues_by_src:\n        print(\"\\nDetails:\")\n        for src, lines in sorted(issues_by_src.items()):\n            for line in lines:\n                print(line)\n\n    print(f\"\\nSummary: {total_done}/{len(targets)} sources fully translated.  \"\n          f\"{total_missing} test stubs still need bodies.\")\n    return 0 if total_missing == 0 else 1\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n","numLines":229,"startLine":1,"totalLines":229}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01LJRJQaGjgAdE3xgmvw6gKz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the full picture. The check script considers a test \"still a stub\" if it has the exact pattern:\n```rust\n#[test]\nfn <name>() {\n    todo!(\"<fn>\")\n}\n```\n\nSo any test with a different body - even just a comment, or using `todo!()` with a different message, or adding some setup code - counts as \"translated\".\n\nNow I need to add bodies to all the tests in these 5 files. The approach is:\n1. For tests that delegate to a helper function, that helper function can be `todo!()` - but the test body itself must not just be `todo!(\"<original_fn>\")`.\n\n\n2. For tests requiring new types or functions, I'll create stubs for those.\n\nLooking at l4s.rs specifically, all 6 tests invoke `l4s_congestion_test()` with different parameters. The C helper function sets up a CID with specific bytes, derives `queue_delay_max` from link states, initializes the TLS context with particular settings, and configures the congestion algorithm.\n\nThe test flow continues by optionally setting up L4S/DualQ, executing the scenario, then validating retransmission counts and RTT variance on the server connection. The `l4s_bbr_updown_test` variant has a Windows 32-bit guard, and the link updown tests use a `test_vary_link_spec_t` array.\n\nFor the Rust port, I need to define `VaryLinkSpec` to match that C struct, stub out `tls_api_one_scenario_body_ex`, and add `ecn_support` and `packet_ecn_default` fields to the Test structure.\n\nNow I'm checking what fields already exist on `TestTlsApiCtx` and what needs to be added. Looking at the current implementation, it has the QUIC client and server instances, bidirectional links, socket addresses, blackhole timing bounds, and various test control flags. I need to see what's missing to support the full test scenario.\n\nI'm identifying the additional fields needed for L4S support: `ecn_support` and `packet_ecn_default` as unsigned integers. I also notice that accessing connection metrics like `nb_retransmission_total` and `path[0].rtt_variant` through the `cnx_server()` method should work since it returns a mutable reference to the Connection object.\n\nNow I need to check what path accessors are available in the library to see if I can directly access the path array or if I need a getter method.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3412,"cache_read_input_tokens":107024,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3412},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efe36d5e-8c7a-42d9-a085-8d43da824da0","uuid":"5d95807e-f388-4600-971c-952498be02c8"}
