{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user invoked a Phase 3A batch translation task: translate C test bodies from `picoquictest/` into Rust `#[test]` bodies under `rs/fq/src/tests/`. The batch covers 5 source files in one session:\n   - `l4s_test` (6 tests: l4s_reno, l4s_prague, l4s_prague_updown, l4s_bbr, l4s_c4, l4s_bbr_updown)\n   - `mbedtls_test` (7 tests: mbedtls, mbedtls_crypto, mbedtls_load_key, mbedtls_load_key_fail, mbedtls_retrieve_pubkey, mbedtls_sign_verify, mbedtls_configure)\n   - `mediatest` (11 tests: video, video_audio, video_data_audio, video2_down, video2_back, video2_probe, wifi, worst, no_coal, suspension, suspension2)\n   - `memlog_test` (1 test: memlog)\n   - `minicrypto_test` (2 tests: minicrypto, minicrypto_is_last)\n   \n   Tests must be faithfully translated with real bodies (not bare `todo!(\"entry_fn\")` stubs). They must compile and naturally panic at the first unimplemented `todo!()` API call. The only authorized production edits are `todo!()` stubs in `rs/fq/src/internal.rs` or `rs/fq/src/lib.rs`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Phase 3A test-body translation: translate C QUIC test bodies to Rust `#[test]` functions\n   - The check script (`scripts/phase3_check.py`) rejects bodies matching the exact pattern `#[test]\\nfn name() {\\n    todo!(\"entry_fn\")\\n}`\n   - Tests may panic at `todo!()` inside API stubs — that is acceptable\n   - L4S (Low Latency, Low Loss, Scalable Throughput) congestion testing with DualQ AQM\n   - mbedTLS backend for picoquic/picotls\n   - Memory performance logging (`auto_memlog`)\n   - Media stream simulation (video, audio, data with frame rates and latency checks)\n   - `TestTlsApiCtx` — combined TLS-API test context holding two QUIC contexts and sim-links\n   - `VaryLinkSpec` — time-varying link bandwidth/latency segments (C: `test_vary_link_spec_t`)\n   - `Dualq::install` — DualQ AQM installation on a sim-link\n   - `CongestionAlgorithm` — congestion control algorithm descriptor\n   - `get_congestion_algorithm(\"name\")` — look up algorithm by string ID\n   - TLS API init flags (`TLS_API_INIT_FLAGS_NO_OPENSSL = 1`, `NO_MINICRYPTO = 2`, `NO_FUSION = 4`)\n   - `reset_tls_api(flags)` — reset TLS provider registry\n   - `Connection::primary_path_rtt_variant()` — RTT variance on primary path (C: `cnx->path[0]->rtt_variant`)\n   - `Connection::memlog_init(nb_records, file_name)` — attach memory log to connection\n   - `is_minicrypto_aes128gcm_sha256(use_low_memory)` / `is_minicrypto_key_loader()` — backend identity checks\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`xlate/test_translation_guide.md`** (read)\n     - Authoritative reference for the Rust API surface, naming conventions, helpers, and translation patterns.\n     - Key: `Quic::new`, `Connection::start_client`, `ConnectionId`, `Instant`, `TestTlsApiCtx`, helper function signatures.\n\n   - **`rs/fq/src/tests/util.rs`** (modified)\n     - Added `ecn_support: u8` and `packet_ecn_default: u8` fields to `TestTlsApiCtx` struct\n     - Updated `cert_verify_set_ctx` constructor: added `ecn_support: 0, packet_ecn_default: 0`\n     - Added `VaryLinkSpec` struct:\n       ```rust\n       #[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy)]\n       pub struct VaryLinkSpec {\n           pub duration: u64,\n           pub bits_per_second_up: u64,\n           pub bits_per_second_down: u64,\n           pub microsec_latency: u64,\n       }\n       ```\n     - Added `tls_api_one_scenario_body_ex` stub:\n       ```rust\n       #[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]\n       pub fn tls_api_one_scenario_body_ex(\n           _test_ctx: &mut TestTlsApiCtx,\n           _simulated_time: &mut Instant,\n           _scenario: &[TestApiStreamDesc],\n           _stream0_target: usize,\n           _init_loss_mask: u64,\n       